  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Special - She Works Here SWOB Grant Facility</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SME.NG Nigerias Impact Investment Platform has designed the SME.NG Women-Owned Business (SWOB) Grant Facility as a direct response to the adverse impact of COVID-19 on women-owned businesses in Nigeria. The goal of the facility is to provide intervention grants to micro and small businesses that are in survival mode to ensure that they recover from the effects of the pandemic. Based on the findings of survey of carried out by SME.NG, the Federal Ministry for Womens Affairs and NACCIMA, the facility will support these businesses in the core areas they expressed challenges such as replenishing stock, establishing supply chains, paying/retaining staff and exploring new revenue streams. Priority will be given to women entrepreneurs in the agri-business, light manufacturing (PPE) and healthcare sectors.</narrative>
  </description>
